# krkr2web: web compact/cache discipline — stop the graphic cache nuke storm.
#
# Device evidence (20260825-051129-299b1ef5): after *gobacktitle the same
# 2MiB window texture (psb://window_cn.pimg/11480.tlg) re-decoded 7 times in
# ~30s with ticks averaging 424ms, and every dialogue-period expression
# change re-decoded its sprites. Instrumented local repro showed the cache
# table EMPTY at every miss (no LRU chops): three paths nuke the whole cache
# on web where re-population costs 50-350ms of main-thread decode per image:
#
# 1. System.doCompact() (game scripts, default level MAX) now clamps to the
#    deactivate level: storage caches still flush (autopath snapshot + XP3
#    archive hold make that cheap), the LRU-capped 160MiB decode cache
#    survives. Allocation-failure GC stays at MAX for real emergencies.
# 2. PNG/JPEG/BMP save paths no longer clear the cache on web (Win9x-era GDI
#    bitmap handle guard; save thumbnails were wiping the cache mid-play).
# 3. Allocation-failure retries (bitmap bits / operator new / memalign) keep
#    delivering MAX compact but now first release the 0088 materialized .root
#    pins (scenario trees, 829k TJS nodes ≈ hundreds of MB near the 1GiB
#    ceiling) via a PSBFile root registry — dropping our reference never
#    breaks the game; trees the script still holds survive via its own refs.
#
# Telemetry: D5_LOAD gains the full search key + cache state (attributes
# misses), D5_CACHE_CLEAR/CHOP log every nuke/eviction, D5_ALLOC_RETRY tags
# the three retry sites, D5_DOCOMPACT_CLAMP and D5_CACHE_CLEAR_SKIPPED_*
# mark the new web behaviors, D5_PSB_ROOT_RELEASE counts emergency releases.
# Local A/B (return-to-title probe): window texture re-decodes 2->0, cache
# grows monotonically (0->117 entries) instead of resetting to 0.
